Original: `const diff = cmd('git diff ' + originBase + '...' + headBranch) || ''; console.log('Diff size (origin fallback):', diff.length, ...)` — logs the RAW capture length (33: 'fallback diff\nCOMMAND_EXIT_CODE=0' = 13+1+19=33? 'COMMAND_EXIT_CODE=0' is 19 chars; 13+1+19 = 33 ✓).

My refactor: `_runDiffCommand` returns `cleanCommandOutput(cmd(...) || '')` — cleaned FIRST, so length is 13. And getPRDiff returns the cleaned diff — same return value. But the LOGGED length differs: original logs raw length, mine logs cleaned length.

Also check the happy path failure (first failed test cut off in output — 'Diff size: 31 chars' vs my 'Diff size: 11 chars'? my refactored logs cleaned 11).

